# The core waits on a faulty slot that CTRL says it can decide: a faulty
# copy at or below the best clean copy never qualifies, so a Phase-1 quorum
# that holds one such copy never decides the slot. The audit's own copy of
# the rule (`audit/losses.rs`, `loss_recoverable`) calls the slot
# recoverable, so it must not excuse the journal: the convergence oracle
# goes red. If the audit's rule were wider than the core's, the slot would
# read as unrecoverable and the run would stay green.
excuse: loss: unrecoverable slot
file: crates/lib/paros-core/src/proposer.rs
--- find
                .is_none_or(|ballot| Some(*ballot) <= threshold)
--- replace
                .is_none()
--- end
